insert into public.tips (id, unit_id, title_en, body_md, status) values
  ('1fb34740-8545-5a6d-a32e-14d71d687456', '465d788e-db67-5a57-8f4e-96306374e29c', 'Yo que vos', '**Yo que vos** — *if I were you* — is how a porteño gives advice, and the conditional follows: **yo que vos, iría**, **yo que vos, no diría nada**.', 'draft'),
  ('e1eabf8c-fd49-53e3-8b04-99a9a67caa72', '465d788e-db67-5a57-8f4e-96306374e29c', '-ía on the whole verb', 'The conditional adds **-ía** to the whole infinitive: *comprar* → **compraría**. A few shorten first: **haría**, **diría**, **tendría**, **podría**.', 'draft'),
  ('70727b15-4913-5e39-a255-0effa794d686', 'ce343377-a0c2-5201-9ff4-824789e73e89', 'Si + a past form + would', 'Something that isn''t true now: **si tuviera plata, viajaría** — *if I had money, I''d travel*. The *si* half uses a new form, **tuviera**, **fuera**, **pudiera**.', 'draft'),
  ('04f23526-26bf-5316-8fb2-a5c912c8462f', 'ce343377-a0c2-5201-9ff4-824789e73e89', 'Only after si', 'You meet this form after *si* and after *ojalá* — **ojalá pudiera** — and almost nowhere else at this level.', 'draft'),
  ('7fef5512-863f-5d20-a29e-02e373792bb2', '41b8c894-067c-540c-88b8-1a334f63f9e2', 'Me gustaría', '**Me gustaría** — *I''d like* — is *gustar* in the conditional, with the same *me*: **me gustaría ir**, **¿te gustaría venir?**. **Me encantaría** is the enthusiastic yes.', 'draft'),
  ('bdb46568-61df-5ccc-b7d5-ca48b6e9195b', 'a973933b-ccb4-5f7d-9210-9a063ab4ed00', 'Manejar, estacionar', 'A porteño **maneja** (drives) an **auto** and spends half an hour trying to **estacionar** (park). *Conducir* and *aparcar* are Spain''s.', 'draft'),
  ('3d16b064-de20-5954-abfd-66692234787d', 'a973933b-ccb4-5f7d-9210-9a063ab4ed00', 'La avenida', 'Buenos Aires is a grid of **avenidas** — Corrientes, Santa Fe, 9 de Julio — and every corner has a **semáforo**. Cross when it''s green: **cruzá**.', 'draft'),
  ('11b0bc61-a2e4-5460-a657-e0879e09a08c', '72e14160-96c0-535c-9819-8ab194bd82cc', 'Cuotas', 'Argentines buy almost anything **en cuotas** — in instalments — and the first question at the till is **¿en cuántas cuotas?**', 'draft'),
  ('b876ba73-9188-5bb8-ab20-2ee24117ccb9', '72e14160-96c0-535c-9819-8ab194bd82cc', 'No me alcanza', '**No me alcanza** — *it''s not enough*, *I can''t make it last*. **Ahorrar** is to save, **gastar** to spend: **gasté todo el sueldo**.', 'draft'),
  ('60f3cec7-feb6-5d7d-87b3-4b4cee709cc5', '2fb39a77-4405-52e0-83ee-a83f56d744ad', 'Dicen que', '**Dicen que** — *they say*, *apparently* — is how a porteño passes on anything heard second-hand. **Parece que** does the same with a shrug.', 'draft'),
  ('df56a42d-f2d8-562e-88b5-84ec61853925', '2fb39a77-4405-52e0-83ee-a83f56d744ad', '¿Viste la noticia?', '**Leí en el diario que…**, **lo vi en la tele** — and **me llamó Sofi y me dijo que…**', 'draft'),
  ('ebd8e8e5-7f3a-581d-ac16-f841077ffb75', 'fa24b60d-3716-5754-bf36-9f5a6843d7bb', 'Buena onda', '**Buena onda** is the porteño compliment for a person: easy, warm, *nice*. **Mala onda** is the opposite. Both stay the same for everyone: *ella es buena onda*.', 'draft'),
  ('6f623f96-84dd-5f21-953b-3e2e7b40775a', 'fa24b60d-3716-5754-bf36-9f5a6843d7bb', 'Pesado', '**Qué pesado** — *what a pain* — for someone who won''t let it go. **Divertido** is *fun*, **tímido** *shy*.', 'draft'),
  ('f7ca6bf1-8ae1-516b-935e-ab0b2f6dcb07', '754cc69f-e7cf-5e64-ba22-2679bc1f609e', '¿Dónde queda?', 'For where a place *is*, porteños say **queda**: **¿dónde queda la farmacia?** — *where''s the chemist?* — and **me queda cerca** — *it''s close to me*.', 'draft'),
  ('9b2c23e3-838a-574f-affd-f711c01a05fe', '754cc69f-e7cf-5e64-ba22-2679bc1f609e', 'Capital y provincia', 'The city is **la Capital**; the ring of towns around it, in the province, is **el conurbano**. Palermo, San Telmo and La Boca are all barrios of the Capital.', 'draft'),
  ('659a6119-e2f6-5433-8d02-6bbaa7f5e7bd', 'aa46af4e-1c1b-50ae-b8c1-03167cabaecc', 'Me preguntó', '**Me preguntó si venía** — *she asked me if I was coming*. **Le contesté que sí** — *I told her yes*. What was said slides into the imperfect.', 'draft'),
  ('c2891689-2f3f-54d4-8ece-c513dcc00952', 'aa46af4e-1c1b-50ae-b8c1-03167cabaecc', 'Vino', '**Vino** is wine, and it is also *he came*: **vino Juan** — *Juan came*. The sentence always tells which.', 'draft'),
  ('c2f1eb75-56ed-521b-8cf9-2a6ca57325cc', '02735212-fad9-5b44-97cb-061657aaad7f', 'The words that glue a conversation', '**Por las dudas** — *just in case*; **de última** — *if all else fails*; **en serio** — *seriously*; **si querés** — *if you like*. Say them and you sound like you''re from here.', 'draft')
